uld say with the exception of the  pomegranate arils which  are rich in antioxidants and fiber i  mean it's got  a whopping seven grams of fiber per cup  her snack choices are pretty high in  salt  so a cup of miso soup has less than 100  calories  but it has 34 of your sodium needs for  the day  that means that a liter of the stuff  will put you  well above your salt targets for the day  and  probably leave you feeling pretty  bloated obviously we know that doritos  and lace chips are going to be high in  salts and saturated fat  but even goldfish which are often touted  as a good option for kids  have 11 of your sodium needs in one  serving  so no shame in enjoying goldfish  crackers i love them or even giving them  to your kids  my kid loves them but to make that snack  a little bit more balanced  i would pair the salty crackers or chips  with a piece of potassium-rich fruit  to help balance that sodium out and if  you want to learn a little bit more  about the relationship between salt  and potassium definitely watch my  nicocado avocado video  right here what else is going on i  am either cooking  probably for stormy or  and myself or girl don't make your own  nutrition an afterthought i get it  though as a busy mom who wants their  kids to eat well  i get that it's totally second nature to  put our kids first  in every area of life and that often  means feeding our kids  before ourselves but when it comes to  food and meals  like i said eating with our littles and  eating the same things  as our kids is actually one of the best  things that we can do for them  the evidence is so clear that family  meals have a wide range of physical  and mental health benefits like better  academic performance  self-esteem and lower risk of depression  eating disorders  obesity and more but it's also one of  the most important and easiest ways  to raise a competent eater so again if  you're looking for  more tips on dealing with picky eating  check out my video  right here as 