for her meals kylie cites  often ordering in  sushi mainly things like sashimi or  spicy avocado tuna on a rice cake which  sounds pretty awesome and i think that  sushi and sashimi  are just inherently really nutritious  takeout options  you know we've got some protein and  healthy omega-3 fats from the fatty fish  like tuna and salmon we've got carbs in  the rice  typically though the only veg that  you'll see in a sushi order  is like that sad iceberg lettuce salad  that they give you  as a side for your meal so to bump up  the fiber in your sushi dinner when you  are ordering  i would recommend opting for brown rice  whenever it's available  getting at least one veggie roll with  things like cucumber and avocado and  carrots and sea  vegetables and then ordering some  edamame or some sauteed  kind of garlic mushrooms on the side i  also recommend opting for really simple  nigeria sashimi or mackie instead of the  really elaborate ones that  are typically packed with tempura bits  and mayo based sauces and things like  that  also i suggest leaning more on things  like wasabi and ginger to flavor your  sushi  rather than soaking it in soy yes low  sodium  soy sauce is a better option than  regular but it still has 22 percent of  your sodium needs per tablespoon  and if you are clumsy with your  chopsticks like i am  it is not hard to just like really get  her soaked i am  definitely not a sushi connoisseur but i  assume if you ask someone who was  they would probably say that if if it is  quality fish  and it probably should be if you're  willing to eat it raw simple  is always best kylie also mentions her  drink choices so she's into corona light  which brings back some unsavory memories  in cancun  also white wine or just like straight up  shots  i mean again i'm not gonna shame any mom  or anyone else for wanting a drink  because  i get it but i'm also not going to  legitimize the health halo  some types of booze like wine is often  given  so my take home on drinking what i call  balanced boozing  is to choose the drink that you enjoy  the most whether that's beer or wine or  spirits  and enjoy it in moderation i  lock myself in my bedroom and  i turn on my tv i get really comfortable  and i pre-slice  an apple find my bed since i'm really  comfortable i'll be too lazy  probably to go down to the kitchen so  i'm gonna  my only choice is this apple so that is  how  i swerve my late night cravings  yeah that is problematic  if you need to lock yourself or a food  up  to prevent yourself from eating then  it's time to really re-evaluate  how you're feeding yourself in the day  an  apple can of course be a great bedtime  snack but  if you're actually wanting popcorn or  toast or  anything else and the only reason that  you're not eating those things is  because you're stuck in your room  you're either a restricting these  forbidden foods and therefore finding  yourself  in a state of mental scarcity b  restricting food in general and are  physically deprived of calories  or c all of the above  so while we are hearing about some fun  foods and kylie's routine like  doritos burgers and beer my sense is  that  these are things that she likes and  wants to eat  but clearly doesn't allow herself to eat  often enough  if she did she wouldn't need to  forcefully limit herself to just  an apple before bed and she also  wouldn't need an official  cheat day to get it all in  so folks i'm sure i probably offended  some of my die hard kardashian fans out  there but  this review was all in fun and it was in  no way intended to critique  kylie personally or professionally in  fact  i have mad respect for a 23 year old  woman  worth a whopping 900 million dollars  i also can say very little about what  kylie eats regularly  or even on like one day since  i'm just going off of this commentary  style harper bazaar video  but if you enjoyed this video and you  want to see me review more of these  harper bazaar clips  please like this video leave me a  comment below on who  i should check out next until then don't  forget to subscribe to the channel  and ring that little bell so you never  miss out on a video  and i will see you next time on abby's  kitchen bye
 

